/-
# Contour data for the Z7 saddle certificate (instance Z7)

Rational vertices of the steepest-descent contour of `h = Re f`, `f = Ψ - 3πi x`:
* the upper polyline `upStart, upPts` (16 vertices) from (the rounding of) `x₀ + ρ d` to `xtop`,
  split into 2 chunks `upC1, …` whose kernel checks live in separate files (`UpChunk*.lean`);
* the lower polyline `dnStart, dnPts` (4 vertices) from (the rounding of) `x₀ - ρ d` down to the
  real point `x_c < 11/12`.

Generated by `scripts/saddle/gen_saddle_Z7.py` (RK4 trace of the steepest-descent ODE from `x₀ ± ρ d`,
`ρ = 1/20`, vertices rounded to `10⁻¹²`, greedy simplification against a float model of the Lean
checks); every claim is re-checked by `decide +kernel` in the files that use this data.

Constants: far threshold `T0 = -10136700000000 / 10 ^ 12` (`Re Ω ≈ -10.1167485`), sector constants `amin = 1/100`,
`Amax = 2.76` (`η = π - 2.76 > 0.38`).
-/
